**Findings.**
- **Docstrings (A-1, A-4)** say exactly what was asked. No deleted var is named any more.
- **Envelope refusal (A-2)** is real. Appending to the rows medium bypasses the encoder's own check, so the throw can only come from the inline consumer loader in test_utils, and a nil result would fail the equality.
- **Blocked writer round trip (A-3)** is real. The wake is now driven from the EDN-revived entry rather than the in-memory one, which is the stronger of the two.
- **Reset (G-1)** is real and stronger than asked. Resetting a halted machine and rerunning to 42 fails if control is not put back at pc 0 or the halted flag is not cleared.
- **Nil origin (G-2)** is real. Slot 1 of a provenance row is the origin, and no default origin would pass it.
- **Blank lines (A-5) is only partly done.** Three triple-blank runs remain in the semantic-register linearize test at lines 230, 326 and 382. HEAD has none. Style only, not a commit gate, so I ledgered it rather than withholding sign-off.

